oracle GNU Make 4.4.1
outcome failure
file Makefile kept 7
| # GNU Make reads every non-switch word in MAKEFLAGS through the same
| # `handle_non_switch_argument` whatever origin it came from, and a word
| # carrying an `=` reaches `parse_variable_definition`, which is fatal on an
| # empty name. `:=` is a word of its own here because the write is unquoted, so
| # this abandons the build before `all` is ever considered.
| MAKEFLAGS += -k := 2
| all: ; @printf 'built\n' > out
